nternship"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For B.Tech/B.E. Industrial Engineering & Management → Operations Analyst, the strongest career positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Industrial Engineering","Operations Research","SQL","Advanced Excel","Power BI","Python","Lean/Six Sigma","Supply Chain","Process Improvement"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should not position themselves only as a traditional industrial engineer. A data-driven Operations Analyst profile—with the ability to connect process efficiency, business KPIs, optimization and analytics—provides broader opportunities across manufacturing, logistics, e-commerce, consulting, technology and other operations-intensive industries."}]}]}